-- title:
--   Level-field node ring as base rational node-ring input
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the set of non-units of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$, and write $A_0 :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the valuation subring $A \cap k_0$ of $k_0$. The hypotheses on the constants are: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, it is a Henselian local ring, its residue field is algebraically closed, and (`hκ`) every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Throughout, $F :=$ `fieldBar q M'` denotes the full-level function field `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$, regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q} \to F$.
--
--   The statement then quantifies over the following data, each subject to the hypotheses listed after it.
--
--   (1) An intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq F$ (the level field) such that $\overline{\mathbb Q} \cdot F_0 = F$, in the form that the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ is all of $F$, and such that the following linear disjointness holds: for every intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$, and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to F$ with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$.
--
--   (2) A valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ which induces $A_0$ on $k_0$ (for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ iff its image in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$), is a discrete valuation ring, and has maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$.
--
--   (3) A subring $O$ of $F_0$, local and noetherian (the node), with: $O \subseteq W_0$; $O$ induces $A_0$ on $k_0$; every $f \in O$ is congruent to a constant, i.e. there is $x \in k_0$ with $x \in A$, image in $O$, and $f - x$ a non-unit of $O$; and $F_0$ is the field of fractions of $O$ in the form that every $f \in F_0$ can be written $f h = g$ with $g, h \in O$, $h \ne 0$.
--
--   (4) A crossing presentation: a natural number $E_0 \ge 1$, a proof that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota_O$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal with parameter the image of $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that crossing model, subject to: $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$; $\iota_O$ carries constants coming from $A_0$ to the corresponding `UVCrossingModel.const`; $\iota_O(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.U` and $\iota_O(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.V`; $c_y \in W_0$ and $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; and $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_0$, lies outside the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) One end of the node: a field $F_I$ with an algebra structure over the residue field of $A$, a `RegularProlongation` $R_x$ of $A$ to $F$ with values in $F_I$ (that is, a valuation subring `Rx.integers` of $F$ inducing $A$ on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $F_I$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$ and satisfying the scaling condition `exists_smul_mem`), and a place $b_x$ of $F_I$ over the residue field of $A$ (a proper valuation subring of $F_I$ containing the constants and a principal ideal ring). The hypotheses are: $b_x$ is rational, i.e. the map from the residue field of $A$ to the residue field of $b_x$ is surjective; $O$ lands in `Rx.integers`; the $R_x$-residues of elements of $O$ lie in the valuation subring of $b_x$; the $R_x$-residue of a non-unit of $O$ lies in the maximal ideal of that valuation subring; the $R_x$-residue of $c_x$ is $0$; and the $b_x$-order of the $R_x$-residue of $c_y$ is $1$.
--
--   (6) The other end: a field $F_{SS}$ over the residue field of $A$, a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ to $F$ with values in $F_{SS}$, and a place $n_d$ of $F_{SS}$ over the residue field of $A$, with: for $f \in F_0$, $f \in R$`.integers` iff $f \in W_0$; $n_d$ is rational; the $R$-residues of elements of $O$ lie in the valuation subring of $n_d$; non-units of $O$ have $R$-residue in its maximal ideal; the $R$-residue of $c_y$ is $0$; and the $n_d$-order of the $R$-residue of $c_x$ is $1$.
--
--   (7) A set $S$ of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ characterised by: $P \in S$ iff $O$ is contained in the valuation subring of $P$ and, for every non-unit $f$ of $O$, the value `P.evalAt` $f$ lies in $A$ and in fact in the maximal ideal of $A$; moreover every $P \in S$ is rational.
--
--   (8) A subring $\mathcal N$ of $F$ characterised as $R_x$`.integers` $\cap\, R$`.integers` $\cap \bigcap_{P \in S} P$`.toValuationSubring`, and such that `P.evalAt` $f \in A$ for all $f \in \mathcal N$ and $P \in S$.
--
--   (9) A subring $C$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ characterised by $c \in C$ iff $c \in A$ and $c$ lies in the bottom intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$, i.e. $C = A \cap k_0$ read in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and a subring $\mathcal N_0$ of $F$ characterised by $f \in \mathcal N_0$ iff $f$ lies in $F_0$ and, as an element of $F_0$, lies in $O$ — that is, $\mathcal N_0$ is $O$ read inside $F$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of instances making $\mathcal N_0$ a local ring and a noetherian ring, together with the conjunction of the following: $S$ is nonempty; $\mathcal N_0 \le \mathcal N$; for every place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $P \in S$ if and only if $\mathcal N_0$ is contained in the valuation subring of $P$ and for every non-unit $f$ of $\mathcal N_0$ the value `P.evalAt` $f$ lies in $A$ and in its maximal ideal; the image of $C$ under $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to F$ is contained in $\mathcal N_0$; every $g \in \mathcal N_0$ admits $o \in C$ whose image lies in $\mathcal N_0$ and with $g - o$ a non-unit of $\mathcal N_0$; for every $n$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $C$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathcal N_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i \cdot a_i = 0$ in $F$ forces all $a_i = 0$; for every $f \in \mathcal N_0$ lying in $R_x$`.integers`, the $b_x$-order of its $R_x$-residue is $\ge 0$, and is $> 0$ when $f$ is a non-unit with non-zero residue; the same statement for $R$ and $n_d$; and finally $c_x$ and $c_y$, read in $F$, lie in $\mathcal N_0$, with the $R_x$-residue of $c_x$ equal to $0$, the $R$-residue of $c_x$ non-zero, the $R$-residue of $c_y$ equal to $0$, and the $R_x$-residue of $c_y$ non-zero (each under the corresponding membership hypothesis for the residue to be defined).
--
--   This is the hypothesis-matching step which takes a node $O$ of the level field $F_0$, with its crossing presentation over the constants $A \cap k_0$ and its two ends (the Igusa-side prolongation $(R_x, b_x)$ and the supersingular-side prolongation $(R, n_d)$), and exhibits the same ring read inside the full-level function field $F$ as an admissible node ring over the constant ring $C = A \cap k_0$: local, noetherian, contained in the intersection of the two integer rings with the places dominating it, cut out by that domination, congruent to constants, linearly disjoint from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $C$, with non-negative orders at the two ends and the opposite vanishing behaviour of the two crossing coordinates. It feeds the layered node-ring constructions [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layerRationalNodeRing_of_baseRationalNodeRing_layer_chart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layerRationalNodeRing_of_baseRationalNodeRing_layer_chart) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layeredRationalNodeRings_of_node_ends_layers`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layeredRationalNodeRings_of_node_ends_layers), and the nonemptiness of $S$ comes from [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_place_mem_toValuationSubring_and_evalAt_mem_maximalIdeal_of_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_place_mem_toValuationSubring_and_evalAt_mem_maximalIdeal_of_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel).
